<Layout title="Cookie Policy — VIRALWIRE" description="VIRALWIRE Cookie Policy.">
<section class="wrap section article">
  <div class="eyebrow">LEGAL</div>
  <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
  <p class="dek">How VIRALWIRE uses cookies and similar browser technologies.</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small files stored by a website in your browser. Similar technologies include local storage and other identifiers that can remember settings or help services understand usage.</p>
    <h2>Essential storage</h2>
    <p>VIRALWIRE may use essential cookies or browser storage for functions such as administration and security. The private Vault Control uses an authentication cookie so an authorized administrator can stay signed in.</p>
    <h2>Preference storage</h2>
    <p>VIRALWIRE uses local storage to remember choices such as dark or light theme, selected language and whether the cookie notice has been dismissed.</p>
    <h2>Advertising and analytics</h2>
    <p>If advertising or analytics services are enabled, third-party providers may use cookies or similar technologies for measurement, personalization or fraud prevention according to their own policies. The exact services enabled on VIRALWIRE may change over time.</p>
    <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
    <p>You can block or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking essential cookies may prevent some functions, including administration, from working correctly.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For questions about cookies used on VIRALWIRE, use the contact method published by VIRALWIRE on its official channels.</p>
    <p><strong>Last updated: September 22, 2026.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>